# Story pipeline — cover → outline → Story Architect → publish

**Goal:** Readers enjoy the books and come back for more. Every fiction book is guided beginning to end — not rushed to published. Educational books (Textbooks / Education / Learning) use the same cover-first discipline but an **instructional** quality path — see `educational-books-pipeline.mdc`.

## Mandatory order (new fiction / prose)

1. **Research / writing brief** — audience, tone, dialogue style, narrative beats (including climax).
2. **Original title gate** — before creating a placer or writing, titles must be original vs the **external world** (Open Library + Google Books), not only our catalog. Classic/public-domain reprints are exempt. Collisions are skipped or auto-renamed (`server/titleOriginality.ts`, `server/titleCollisionRepair.ts`).
3. **Cover first** — publishable cover in Cover Review (`checkStoryWritingGate` blocks writing without it).
4. **Outline** — detailed blueprint: hook, character arcs, genre beats, climax, resolution.
5. **Editorial Brief** — outline scored before prose; fiction must score ≥ 6 or outline is regenerated (max 3 attempts).
6. **Cover ↔ outline cross-exam** — align visual promise with story before chapters.
7. **Story Architect** — bestselling-author techniques assigned per chapter from the outline.
8. **Chapter writing** — prose follows outline, cover, and writing brief.
9. **Illustrations (visual genres)** — placement and captions come from the **outline** / pipeline before generation. Do not invent random art after the fact.
10. **Strict quality gate** — structural + genre + dialogue; fiction also checks climax (score ≥ 6).
11. **Ready → publish** — only after strict gate passes.

### Title collision repair (existing AI books)

If an EbookGamez-authored title matches (or near-matches) a real-world book: rename → regenerate cover **the same way** (prefer `coverStyleId`) → republish. Do not leave colliding AI titles live. Script: `script/repair-title-collisions.ts`.

### Illustration backtrack policy (existing art)

- **Keep** images that are already generated if they relate to the characters / storyline at all.
- **Replace only** when an image has **nothing to do** with the story or characters (e.g. telescope, microscope, textbook diagram, wrong-world art).
- Do **not** regen for mild beat mismatch, imperfect composition, or “could be more precise.”
- Going forward: new illustrations must be **outline/pipeline pre-approved** before generation.

## Educational books (school / college / trade)

Same cover-first order, but: instructional outline + blocking educational editorial brief ≥ 6; strict gate uses **instructional materials** check (no climax); pedagogy scan for objectives/examples/practice. Details in `educational-books-pipeline.mdc` and `shared/educationalBookQuality.ts`.

### Page layout (research verdict)

**Not necessary:** fixed two-column print-textbook typesetting (digital HQIM uses reflowable EPUB/web + WCAG accessibility).

**Necessary and added:** schoolbook reader chrome — labeled section callouts (Objectives / Example / Practice / Check / Key Terms) + inline diagrams that share the page with lesson text (`usesSchoolbookPageLayout` in the flipbook reader).

## Never shortcut (unless user explicitly asks)

- Do **not** start content generation without cover (except resume of substantial in-progress work).
- Do **not** use structural-only gates to promote or publish fiction.
- Do **not** bypass outline / Story Architect for “fast fixes” — repair chapters, then re-run **strict** gate.
- Do **not** apply fiction climax checks to Textbooks / Education / Learning.
- Overnight / batch scripts must use **`runPublishPipelineGate(d, { strict: true })`**.

## Repair workflow

Fix the problem → **`audit-one-draft.ts <id>`** (strict by default) → promote only if pass → publish.

Structural-only audit: `audit-one-draft.ts <id> --structural-only` (exception path only).

